<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's Comanav has new ferry on Spain service.</title>
<headline>Morocco's Comanav has new ferry on Spain service.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's Compagnie de Navigation Maritime (Comanav) has launched a new ferry on its service linking the northern city of Tangier to southern Spain, MAP news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>The new ferry, called El Mansour, will daily cross the Gibraltar straits transporting up to 1,300 passengers and 450 vehicles to Algesiras in southern Spain, the agency said.</p>
<p>Morocco, which plans to expand its seas links with southern Europe, has regular services to Algesiras and to Sete, France.</p>
<p>- Newsroom +212-7 72 65 18</p>
